open_wmemstream's write converted its bytes only while it had room for
the characters it counted of them, so the bytes a stream's buffer ended
with inside a character were not taken into the state: the stream wrote
them alone next, which took none, an error, and fputwc failed wherever a
character of more bytes than one crossed the buffer's end. The write
goes on to the end of its bytes; an incomplete character's bytes stay in
the state, as mbrtowc keeps them, and make no character.

--- a/lib/libc/stdio/open_wmemstream.c
+++ b/lib/libc/stdio/open_wmemstream.c
@@ -137,7 +137,7 @@
 	 * characters.
 	 */
 	consumed = 0;
-	while (len > 0 && ms->offset < ms->len) {
+	while (len > 0) {
 		charlen = mbrtowc(*ms->bufp + ms->offset, buf, len,
 		    &ms->mbstate);
 		if (charlen == (size_t)-1) {
